course: dictionary
lesson: 2320
title: Words for feelings: crossness
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Crossness is a noun, a word for a feeling. It is the state of being cross, which means annoyed or a bit angry. Cross is the describing word: «She was cross with her brother.» Crossness names that same feeling as a thing.
explain: Crossness is a smaller feeling than fury. You are not shouting or stamping, just irritated. «Her crossness passed» means the annoyed feeling went away. «With a hint of crossness» means only a little of it could be seen or heard.
explain: Spot the word by its ending. Cross becomes crossness when you add -ness, just as kind becomes kindness and sad becomes sadness. When -ness is added to a feeling word, it usually names that feeling.
fact: Crossness means the feeling of being cross: annoyed or a bit angry.
fact: «Cross» is the describing word; crossness is the noun that names the feeling.
fact: Crossness is uncountable, so you cannot say «a crossness» or «two crossnesses»; say «some crossness».
fact: «Her crossness passed» means her annoyed feeling went away.
fact: In «signs are shaking, sweating, paleness, crossness or confusion», crossness is one sign that someone's blood sugar is too low.
exercise: «With a hint of crossness, he closed the door.» What does crossness mean here? | Being very tired after a long day | Loud singing in the street | *A little annoyance | A big party with music
exercise: In «her crossness passed», which word is the describing word that goes with crossness? | crossing | *cross | crossword | crossed
exercise: Ella says crossness is just another word for fury. Is she right? | Yes, but only when you are at the seaside | *No, crossness is milder, a bit annoyed rather than furious | Yes, they mean exactly the same thing | No, crossness means happy and calm
test: «The baby's crossness grew as the wait got longer.» What is crossness? | *Annoyance or a bit of anger | A type of cake | A kind of sleep | Happiness that lasts all day
test: Which word is the noun for the feeling of being cross? | cross | *crossness | crossly | crossed
exam: Choose the best word for the gap: «Her ___ showed in her frown, but she did not shout.» | *crossness | crossed | cross | crossly
